---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Better Pila — Independent Civic Transparency"
  description="Learn who Better Pila serves, our principles, and how this independent public records project operates in Pila, Laguna."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span>
        <span>About</span>
      </div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The Project</p>
      <h1>Public records should be clear, sourced, and easy to find.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Better Pila is an independent civic portal organizing publicly available municipal records in Pila, Laguna to promote civic literacy and government transparency.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section narrow">
    <article class="paper content">
      <div class="notice" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Non-Governmental Civic Notice:</strong> Better Pila is an independent, non-partisan public records initiative maintained by citizens and researchers. It is not affiliated with, operated by, or funded by the Municipal Government of Pila, the Provincial Government of Laguna, or any political party.
      </div>

      <h2 style="color: var(--navy-deep); margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">The Town of Pila & Civic Heritage</h2>
      <p>
        The historic municipality of Pila, Laguna carries a distinguished tradition of civic and cultural heritage. Formally designated as a <strong>National Historical Landmark</strong> by the National Historical Institute (now NHCP) in 2000, Pila’s centuries-old Spanish colonial town plaza layout, ancestral heritage homes, and the historic San Antonio de Padua parish (established 1578) demonstrate an enduring commitment to community and order.
      </p>
      <p>
        Spanning 17 barangays—from the lakefront farming communities of Linga, Aplaya, and Pinagbayanan to the central town districts of Santa Clara, Bulilan, and Labuin—the citizens of Pila deserve clear, reliable access to the public records that govern their lives.
      </p>

      <h2 style="color: var(--navy-deep); margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">What Better Pila is</h2>
      <p>
        Better Pila is a public-interest digital archive dedicated to organizing, indexing, and contextualizing public government information for the Bayan ng Pila. We track certified legislative acts of the Sangguniang Bayan, municipal executive offices, official budget authorizations (including the Annual Investment Program), infrastructure expenditures, and local administrative contacts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our purpose is civic empowerment: enabling residents, youth leaders, local business owners, researchers, and civil society organizations to easily navigate municipal processes, understand fiscal allocations, and participate meaningfully in local governance.
      </p>

      <div style="background: var(--paper-subtle); border-left: 4px solid var(--navy-2); border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0; padding: 1.4rem; margin: 2rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left-width: 4px;">
        <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--navy-deep);">Statutory Foundations for Transparency</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.6;">
          Better Pila operates under the foundational legal principles of Philippine freedom of information and local autonomy:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.9rem; display: grid; gap: 0.45rem;">
          <li><strong>1987 Philippine Constitution (Art. III, Sec. 7):</strong> Guaranteed right of the people to information on matters of public concern.</li>
          <li><strong>Republic Act No. 7160 (Local Government Code of 1991):</strong> Mandated transparency in municipal ordinances, budgets, and public contracts.</li>
          <li><strong>DILG Full Disclosure Policy (FDP):</strong> Requirement for local government units to publicly post financial documents, bids, and budgets.</li>
          <li><strong>Executive Order No. 2, s. 2016:</strong> Operationalizing freedom of information and public disclosure protocols.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 style="color: var(--navy-deep); margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">What Better Pila is not</h2>
      <p>
        Better Pila is not a government agency. We do not issue business permits, process barangay clearances, accept local real property taxes, or speak on behalf of municipal officials. For official legal, business, or government proceedings, always consult the responsible municipal department and certified primary copies.
      </p>

      <h2 style="color: var(--navy-deep); margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">Editorial Independence & Volunteers</h2>
      <p>
        The archive is maintained by volunteer civic technologists, researchers, and community members with ancestral roots and family in Pila, Laguna. We adhere strictly to non-partisan reporting, source-backed evidence, and visible verification dates.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.8rem;">
        <a href="/methodology" class="button button-primary">Read research methodology →</a>
        <a href="/corrections" class="button button-secondary">Submit a verified correction</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
